--- !u!114 &206742868
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 206742865}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The junkie was waiting in the exact same spot. He snatched the watch and
    bit the metal to test it\u2014what a total imbecile. He handed me a box wrapped
    in some filthy newspaper and bailed without even saying 'later.'\r\nI flew up
    the stairs two at a time, clutching that heavy hunk of iron to my chest like
    it held my entire new life. I hooked it up fast. The old 'Elektron' TV put up
    a fight, spitting snow across the screen while I twisted the stupid channel-tuning
    knob. And then, the sound kicked in\u2014a low hum that made the floor vibrate.\r\nThe
    <b>PERSON 2</b> logo drifted out of the darkness of the picture tube, and I finally
    let out a breath. I remembered the guys dragging me to a gaming club once\u2014it
    reeked of cigarettes and sweat in there. The games there were in color, all bright
    and flashy, but on my screen... everything was black and white, grainy as hell.
    But I actually dig it. There\u2019s something about it.\n\r\n<size=90%>I\u2019m
    writing this sitting on the floor in the hallway because I\u2019ve been kicked
    out of the room. Mom didn't come home alone\u2014she brought some guy with her.
    He reeks of cheap beer and even cheaper cigarettes. First, they were scarfing
    down food in the kitchen, clattering around, and now they\u2019ve locked themselves
    in the living room where the TV is.They kicked me out like I\u2019m some kind
    of stray dog; they even booted the poor cat into the bathroom. I can hear them
    in there, braying with laughter and the bed creaking. But I don\u2019t even give
    a fuck anymore. I managed to snatch the console and hide it under my bed.The
    main thing is, that junkie stuffed five whole cartridges into the box. One says
    something about labyrinths; the others don\u2019t even have labels, just bare
    plastic. I wonder what kind of GAMES are on them. Maybe there\u2019s something
    in there that lets you disappear from this apartment for good.</size>\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 45ae1b20a8af0b947bf46692f07a66b7, type: 2}
