  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "But then the TV-guy just punched me in the gut. Wordlessly. All that perfect
    radiance in my head suddenly sparked and cracked like an old monitor. He just
    switched off this 'divine' dictation with a single move. And instead of perfect
    plans, I suddenly felt the stink of my own sneakers, the burn of the scrape on
    my elbow, how much I just wanted to scream and punch the wall. He didn't explain;
    he just slammed on the gas. My hand broke free on its own and started drawing
    a giant, toothed maw right over the straight lines. Thickly, until the paper
    tore. It\u2019s like this guy in the TV is telling me: 'What fucking eternity?
    You're alive! You had a blast running in the mud! It was fun for you to just
    draw monsters!' The Principal went silent, like her wires were cut. I\u2019m
    sitting here, breathing hard, and I feel something angry, hairy, and very real
    waking up inside me. Something that doesn't want to be a genius. Something that
    just wants to be itself."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 45ae1b20a8af0b947bf46692f07a66b7, type: 2}
